I(1,[1,2],6,[38,40],[[1,14]],'title, date or page count','Gribouillis de Tate sur sa théorie; Questions diverses en théorie de Tate-Hodge','Two headings identify an archival packet associated with Tate and a question sheet on Tate–Hodge theory; they do not establish that Tate wrote every enclosed leaf.','No handwriting attribution is possible without scans.','agrees','The notes accurately distinguish the heading from authorship and retain the foliation as editorial evidence.')
I(2,[3,6,17,18,19],6,[41,45],[[18,37],[133,166]],'conjecture','Conjecture; On a un isom canonique','For a smooth proper variety X over a mixed-characteristic complete discretely valued field K, with C the completed algebraic closure and G_K its Galois group, seek a functorial Hodge–Tate decomposition H^n_et(X_C,Q_p)⊗C ≅ ⊕_{a+b=n}H^b(X,Ω^a)⊗C(−a), compatible with products and cycle classes. The earlier page additionally asks for a filtered de Rham/Hodge splitting.','The modern p-adic field, smoothness/properness and interpretation of H_B are reconstructed from the continuous discussion, not all repeated on either sheet. A Hodge–Tate decomposition does not itself canonically split the filtered de Rham space.','agrees','The explicit conjecture and cycle-compatibility equation are present. Note ##6 is a question/request to construct, not an established theorem.',{6:('corrected','The heading Construire/Conditions and surrounding questions make this a requested construction, not an asserted unproved result.')})
I(3,[4],6,[41],[[25,26]],'conjecture','Tout Q_ell(pi)-module simple ... est-il contenu dans un C(i) ?','Two questions: must every finite-dimensional irreducible continuous Q_p-representation of G_K embed in one C_p(i), and can both M and M(i), i≠0, embed in C_p?','The identification ell=p and pi=G_K uses the Tate–Hodge setting. Distinguish arbitrary continuous representations from those arising geometrically.','agrees','The two question marks describe two different assertions and neither is answered on this page.')
I(4,[5],6,[41],[[28,32]],'conjecture',"Y-a-t-il d'autres conditions ... que celles résultant de la conjecture de Tate ?",'Determine further necessary constraints on the Galois representation H^i_et(X_C,Q_p), beyond the unnamed Tate conjecture being invoked.','The manuscript does not specify exactly which Tate conjecture or the geometric category; no unique strongest classification statement is extractable.','agrees','The notes correctly retain the missing specification rather than supplying a conjecture from context.')
