I(18,[43,44,45,46,47,48],6,[56,57],[[364,404]],'unproved claim','intersection complète, donc Gorenstein; M_réd ... lisse sur k','At an ordinary polarized abelian variety of dimension g over a perfect field of characteristic p, the formal polarized deformation problem is a multiplicative-type kernel. Over an algebraically closed field this gives complete-intersection Cohen–Macaulay/Gorenstein local rings, locally irreducible with smooth reduced ring; the dimension is g(g+1)/2, and prime-to-p polarization yields smoothness.','A level structure sufficient for a fine moduli scheme, or the deformation functor, is required: a coarse quotient can introduce singularities. The manuscript retains a cancelled flatness doubt, so mixed-characteristic flatness is not certified here.','agrees','The explicit restriction to ordinary varieties, the cancellation, dimension, and prime-to-p qualification are all present and must stay attached.')
I(19,[49,50,51,52],6,[59],[[407,472]],'unproved claim','Ext^1(G_a,G_a) ... A[F]-module libre ... à gauche','Over S=Spec A of characteristic p, commutative fppf extensions of G_a by G_a form the stated Frobenius-skew module generated by the length-two Witt extension. For H=G_a or the indicated finite locally free additive subgroup, restriction to W_1, vanishing of V-transition maps, and generation by W_(n+1) are asserted.','Sheaf Ext and global Ext are not interchangeable; the underlining varies. The displayed map a_2 lacks an identified arrow, and the left/right conventions act in different Ext variables. All such conventions are retained as unresolved where not specified.','agrees','The notes accurately distinguish the four parts and the two explicit Demazure–Gabriel locators; a blanket “proved” status would overstate the abbreviated induction.')
I(20,[53],6,[59],[[412,472]],'idea of the earlier run','à gauche; à droite','The earlier run uses F∘[t]=[t^2]∘F over F_2[t] to diagnose the two skew module actions on extension classes.','The polynomial identity is verified here; reconciling all Ext conventions still requires the diagrams, not merely this identity.','agrees','The idea labels its elementary calculation and its proposed extension separately.')
I(21,[54],6,[60],[[475,485]],'withdrawn in the same text','Question ... Ext^1(H,W)=0 ?? Non déjà pour H=alpha_p','Local sheaf-Ext vanishing does not imply vanishing of global Ext on an affine imperfect field: the author immediately rejects that inference using H=alpha_p.','To verify the exact counterexample one must specify the Witt direct system and compute its Hom sheaf; the familiar fppf H^1(k,alpha_p)=k/k^p is relevant but is not automatically the same Ext group.','agrees','The note records the author’s “Non”; recategorize the heading from conjecture to a withdrawn question.',{54:('corrected','The page immediately answers the question negatively; it is not an outstanding conjecture.')})
I(22,[55,56],6,[60],[[487,531]],'withdrawn in the same text','G se dévisse en groupes isom. à alpha_p','For a finite commutative radicial unipotent group over a possibly imperfect characteristic-p field, the live assertion is sheaf Ext^1(G,colim_V W_n)=0 via alpha_p dévissage. The smooth affine-space description of Hom(G,W_n) and the Dieudonné relations below it are wholly cancelled.','The local filtration/descent needed over an imperfect field must be checked; the cancellation must not erase the still-live part (b).','agrees','The note correctly separates live (b) from deleted (a), its induction and §5. Mathematical status is recorded separately for those layers.')
I(23,[57,58,59,60],6,[61],[[534,594]],'self-flagged step','s’étend de façon unique; anti-équivalence ... vérifier','Finite étale p-power torsion groups extend uniquely across nilpotent thickenings. Tensoring their dual Z/p^n-local systems with the structure crystal gives unit-root F-crystals; at a fixed free level the author asks to verify anti-equivalence, and extends it locally to sums of different levels. Sections are recovered as Frobenius-compatible maps to the unit crystal.','The exact category and level conditions must be retained. V=pF^{-1} is automatic only when F is invertible, and a finite locally free coefficient hypothesis is needed.','agrees','The marginal vérifier governs the categorical assertion. The earlier construction is well specified, but its converse/descent are not proved on the leaf.')
I(24,[61,63],6,[62],[[596,617]],'reading question','RHom_Z(G,O_S) ≃ check G ⊗^L_Z O_S','For finite étale G killed by p^n, the cotangent complex vanishes; the remaining duality triangle is related to its constant-sheaf dual. The printed RHom-to-derived-tensor equality needs a degree-convention check.','Under usual cohomological grading and check G=Hom(G,Q_p/Z_p), RHom_Z(G,O) ≃ (check G⊗^L_Z O)[−1]. For G=Z/p and O=F_p the degrees differ without that shift. The underlying triangle’s convention is not silently repaired.','understates','The notes notice dual notation but miss the shift test; add a high-dependency scan reading alert.',{61:('corrected','The unshifted derived Hom/tensor equality fails in the elementary Z/p test under standard cohomological conventions; determine the manuscript convention on the ink.'),63:('kept','check G is the constant p-primary dual, while G* is Cartier dual; both occur and should not be harmonized.')})
I(25,[62,64,65],6,[62,63],[[619,685]],'unproved claim','V ... est un isomorphisme; un hom ... est nul','Cartier duality carries finite étale p-primary groups to multiplicative-type groups; the latter correspond to crystals with invertible V. Morphisms from connected multiplicative p-groups to étale groups vanish, as do the corresponding contravariant F- or V-compatible crystal maps by invertible-versus-nilpotent iteration. The reverse-direction heading has no argument.','Over a nonreduced base an étale→multiplicative morphism need not vanish; the missing part (b) must not be filled by symmetry. For example over F_p[epsilon]/epsilon^p, 1↦1+epsilon defines Z/p→mu_p.','agrees','The notes distinguish the one proved direction from the empty reverse-direction heading.')
I(26,[66,67,68,69],6,[65,66],[[687,755]],'unproved claim','Le foncteur phi est une équivalence de catégories','For any characteristic-p scheme S, finite étale F_p-local systems of finite rank are equivalent to finite locally free O_S-modules M with a Frobenius-linear isomorphism F_S^*M→M. The inverse is the kernel of x↦F(x^p)−x; geometric fibres have p^rank(M) elements and span M.','Finite rank is supplied as an explicit necessary qualification to “loc. libres”; the proof of finiteness is stronger than “étale with constant rank”: locally monic p-power equations give a finite free algebra.','agrees','The page sketches full faithfulness via Artin–Schreier and reduces essential surjectivity to a fixed-vector lemma, which is stated without proof.')
I(27,[70,71],6,[66],[[762,792]],'unproved claim','Zar ou fppf, c’est kif kif','Proposed extension from F_p-local systems to finite p-primary étale groups via Witt modules locally sums of W_n, and their representing smooth Witt-module schemes.','The last category is only described as smooth W-module schemes and is too broad without the bounded length and Frobenius conditions. Equivalence is not asserted here under a completely specified category.','agrees','The note is a correct warning that the diagram and descent conventions are unfinished.')
I(28,[72],6,[66],[[751,755]],'idea of the earlier run','E⊗_(F_p)k ≃ M','In rank one over Fbar_2 with Frobenius x↦x², the fixed subspace is F_2 and extension of scalars recovers k.','This finite example is the earlier run’s calculation and is not a proof of the general semilinear fixed-basis lemma.','agrees','The note’s limited confidence is appropriate; its maps have been checked.')

